    56	
    57	**Given:** ZF. Neither statement is assumed; the theorem asserts their equivalence.
    58	
    59	[L1] For every set $A$ there is a least ordinal $\aleph(A)$ admitting no injection into $A$, and its construction is choice free ([[thm-hartogs]]).
    60	
    61	[L2] Over ZF the Axiom of Choice is equivalent to the well-ordering theorem, that every set can be well ordered ([[cor-ac-iff-well-ordering]], [[def-well-order]]).
